 34AR c  Phys. Rev. C 97, 015802 (2018)                                         
 34AR c  Compiled by S. Ota (NNDC,BNL)   July 18, 2022                          
 34AR c  A {+30}S beam produced using the {+3}He({+28}Si,{+30}S)n reaction was  
 34AR2c  separated with the CRIB separator in RIKEN and sent into the active    
 34AR3c  target filled with {+nat}He+Co{-2} gas (90% and 10% by volume,         
 34AR4c  respectively).  The {+30}S beam energy is 48.4 ({I20}) MeV at the      
 34AR5c  target entrance behind the two PPACs (beamline monitors) and a thin    
 34AR6c  Kapton foil. The target pressure is 194.2 ({I5}) Torr. The |a          
 34AR7c  particles from the elastic scattering were measured with Si telescope  
 34AR8c  arrays. The center-of-mass energy was deduced from the energy and      
 34AR9c  angle of the |a particles, and the excitation function of the {+30}S   
 34ARac  elastic scattering cross sections on {+4}He was measured at            
 34ARbc  E{-c.m.}=2.0-5.5 MeV. Energies, spin-parity, and |a, p partial widths  
 34ARcc  of three resonances in {+34}Ar were deduced using the R-Matrix         
 34ARdc  analysis.                                                              
